WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.430
In 2024, cocoa futures
passed 10,000 dollars a tonne

2
00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:08.480
for the first time, after
poor harvests in West Africa.

3
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.950
Crop prices lurch like this often.

4
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:15.030
Weather, pests and disease
shift supply without warning.

5
00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.760
Now picture the opposite.

6
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.960
A perfect growing season,
and a bumper crop.

7
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.120
Farmers should be celebrating.

8
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.820
Many are not.

9
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.620
So why can a huge harvest
leave farmers with less

10
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.380
money than a small one?

11
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.800
In this mission, you'll compare crops
and metals with factory-made products,

12
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.820
and see why their prices
behave so differently.

13
00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.510
Then you'll work out
the revenue from a poor,

14
00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:41.100
a normal and a bumper harvest.

15
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.270
Your mission: find out
why a good year for crops

16
00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.110
can be a bad year for farmers.
